      "body": [
       {
        "en": "Nadia can tell the sponsorship story beautifully on Tuesday. On Friday, at Level 4 (Hiring Manager persona, shuffled set, guidance off), it comes third instead of first, after a question about a mistake, and she cannot find the opening sentence she has been using. She stalls for four seconds, then starts from the number: “Rp 25 juta, enam belas hari.” The story comes out in a different order, shorter, with the reason before the action, and the probe “kenapa enam orang, bukan seluruh panitia?” finds an answer because the reason was practised as a fact on Day 2.",
        "id": "Hari Selasa, Nadia bisa menceritakan kisah sponsorship-nya dengan sangat baik. Hari Jumat, di Tingkat 4 (persona Hiring Manager, set diacak, panduan mati), cerita itu muncul di urutan ketiga, bukan pertama, setelah pertanyaan soal kesalahan, dan ia tidak bisa menemukan kalimat pembuka yang biasa ia pakai. Ia terdiam empat detik, lalu mulai dari angkanya: “Rp 25 juta, enam belas hari.” Ceritanya keluar dengan urutan berbeda, lebih pendek, dengan alasan sebelum tindakan, dan galian “kenapa enam orang, bukan seluruh panitia?” menemukan jawabannya, karena alasan itu sudah dilatih sebagai fakta di Hari 2."
       },
       {
        "en": "Her improvement log for the session says: “Opening sentence was a script, gone under shuffle. Story held from the facts. Fix: rehearse the first ten seconds five ways, never one.” That is the lesson of the ladder: Level 2 would have told her the story was ready. Level 4 told her which part was a script.",
        "id": "Catatan perbaikannya untuk sesi itu berbunyi: “Kalimat pembuka ternyata naskah, hilang saat diacak. Ceritanya bertahan karena faktanya. Perbaikan: latih sepuluh detik pertama dengan lima cara, jangan cuma satu.” Itulah pelajaran dari tangga realisme: Tingkat 2 akan bilang ceritanya sudah siap. Tingkat 4 memberi tahu bagian mana yang ternyata naskah."
       }
      ]
